  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 236 PM EDT Mon Oct 26 2026\n\nNow - Friday Night...\n\nDry conditions will persist through the entire work week as high \npressure and upper ridging dominate the pattern. The upper ridge \ndoes break down briefly mid week, and a weak and moisture starved \nshortwave passes through the flow early Wednesday. However, with dry \nair in place doubt we'd see more than an increase in mid to upper \nlevel sky cover with this feature.\n\nShould mostly be a persistence forecast this week, outside of \nslightly warmer temps by the end of the week thanks to better SW \nflow on the back side of retreating surface high pressure. Highs \nwill mostly be in the mid 70s through Wednesday, and then in the \nupper 70s by Thursday and Friday. Chilly mornings will continue with \nlows mostly in the 40s. One exception will be early Wednesday \nmorning when the increased cloud cover associated with the \naforementioned shortwave will keep temps a bit milder in the low 50s. \nIn addition to the chilly temperatures, river valley fog will be \nprominent each morning outside of Wednesday morning. Again, because \nof notably increased sky cover.\n\nThe main themes during this prolonged dry stretch continue to be \nworsening drought conditions, and any fire weather concerns. A call \nwith fire partners today revealed the small fuels are still not all \nthat concerning given good RH recovery each night. That being said, \nanother week of drying combined with slightly better wind flow late \nweek could lead to a few wildfire concerns.\n\nSaturday - Monday...\n\nThe upper ridge axis and surface high pressure shift eastward going \ninto the weekend, and focus will shift upstream to western and \ncentral CONUS troughing and potentially multiple strong shortwaves \nejecting out. Our earliest rain chances (fairly low) arrive on \nSaturday, however the better chances will be Saturday night into \nSunday as the lead shortwave ejects out. Still not a lot of clarity \nwith this system, but again, there has been a consistent signal for \nprecip chances at least in the likely range 60-80%. Could have a \nbrief lull in active weather on Monday between the lead wave and \nanother potent anomaly set to arrive more in the mid week time \nframe. Overall, temps trend a bit cooler through this period given \nthe increased cloud cover and precipitation, however we will likely \nstill be above normal for this time of year in the low 70s.",
